           I started playing nethack during the winter break and man i
was hooked to it. Choosing which class to play, I look toward wikihack
to find answers. Choosing valkyrie (easiest job), I concentrated on
using its high constitution and strength to plow down enemies. But
every time i got closer, i usually died for stupid reason (one known
for leaving a cockatrice corpse on the ground to be eventually carried
by a yendorian soldier). But i continue to go foward death after death
learning from these stupid mistakes.

           On October 22, I started my neutral valkyrie with 18
strength and constitution, perfect for an early start. Went to the
mines to find some armor before going to sokoban. I got lucky and got
+3 shoes and +5 dwarvish cloak. I went to sokoban,solve the puzzle
with no problem and gotten the amulet reflection. Went back to the
mines to get the luckstone and to find more enchant armor. Luckily,
through time, i found a +3 leather gloves. The dungeon onward was
repetitive and a rare occasion of not finding a single leprechaun hall
or even a scroll of enchant armor.

           At one point i was lucky to find a wand of wishing inside a
chest outside of the castle. I got my dragon armor, genocided all
Liches and all "h" which would make the castle much easier. Going to
the castle, i skipped the porticullus and used my ring of levitation
to cross the water and used the holes to make all non-flying enemies
fall to the graveyard. I got the other wand of wishing and got the
loot in Fort Ludios afterso. With the right level, i went to the quest
to get the bell. The transition to Gehemnon wasn't difficult and was
the lazy part of the game. I was fortunate to stone Orcus and get his
WoD, get the candle-holder (can't really spell it), and get two
amulets of life-saving. Before getting the BotD, I thought it was
ideal to find the vibrating square first to prevent wasting time
finding with Rodney behind my back. I went to get the book and went
back to the square with Rodney appearing once and non of my items
cursed.

          Getting the Amulet was hard to get. I was almost killed and
nearly used up my AoLS. Embarassingly, i was fighting him with my
pickaxe without noticing it and was fortunate to switch weapons and
quickly kill him. I got the amulet and quickly ran out, (Note, it is
very smart to make a quick path from stairs to stairs so that you can
go up to the end game faster). I quickly got to the Planes with Rodney
appearing twice, which i killed him quickly with WoD.

          The planes weren't as hard as I first thought. The only
concern i had was an Archon in the Planes of Air, but other than that,
i used scrolls of gold detection while confused to find the portals
and ran to it.

         The Astral Plane was here and i was ready to win. Sadly, i
kind of cheated by using the astral call cheat, but i was fortunate to
find myself going to the altar at DEATH side. I slowly squeezed
through the angels, priests and even ignoring death at the risk of
losing both my amulets to get to the end. Luckily, Death was surround
by weak monsters summoned by priests and i safely walked to the altar.
Getting "two bits for an ale", I offered it to Odin, and saw the most
satisfying typed-ending in my life.

         Some noticable things about the ascension:

         never polymorphed or polypile
         didn't wished for artifacts
         genocided 13 monsters


